WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.069 --> 00:00:02.069
Hey guys, Jan here!

00:00:02.069 --> 00:00:05.400
I hope you've had a chance to watch Daredevil
Season 2!

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:10.460
Just like season 1, I really enjoyed it and
loved Jon Bernthal's Punisher and Elodie Yung's

00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:11.460
Elektra.

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:15.879
There were so many cool storylines explored
and lots of teases to possible future characters

00:00:15.879 --> 00:00:17.679
and plot lines left open for the future.

00:00:17.679 --> 00:00:23.450
So, I wanted to look at 7 things I really
want to see in Daredevil Season 3 and future

00:00:23.450 --> 00:00:25.150
Marvel Netflix shows!

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:29.200
And spoiler warning: if you haven't finished
Daredevil Season 2 yet, make sure you come

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:33.710
back after you have, or you can check out
my spoiler-free review here!

00:00:33.710 --> 00:00:38.670
With that very cool closing shot in the season
2 finale, it seems almost guaranteed that

00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:42.770
we'll see Elektra revived by The Hand, but
I'm wondering in what form she's going to

00:00:42.770 --> 00:00:43.770
come back.

00:00:43.770 --> 00:00:48.129
In the comics, when the Hand goes to resurrect
Elektra, it orders its ninjas to give their

00:00:48.129 --> 00:00:52.680
blood for her, and in the TV show we had the
kidnapped children being tapped for their

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:53.680
blood.

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:57.090
I'd love to see if Elektra will be used as
a kind of host for the Beast which is what

00:00:57.090 --> 00:01:01.559
the Hand might have been digging for with
that huge hole in the middle of Manhattan.

00:01:01.559 --> 00:01:05.860
In the comics, The Beast is a an ancient demon
that The Hand worships and in the Shadowland

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:10.540
story arc Daredevil becomes possessed by The
Beast so doing the same with Elektra on the

00:01:10.540 --> 00:01:12.750
TV show could be a cool twist.

00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:17.380
Melvin Potter, Daredevil's costumer, has had
some great scenes so far and both Daredevil

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:22.240
seasons have teased Potter's alter-ego Gladiator
from the comics with tons of easter eggs scattered

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:23.730
around his workshop.

00:01:23.730 --> 00:01:28.790
There's the gladiators movie poster, the circular
saws that Gladiator uses as weapons, the blueprints

00:01:28.790 --> 00:01:32.990
for a new costume, and Melvin's tease of his
classic Gladiator symbol which he revealed

00:01:32.990 --> 00:01:34.399
to Matt in season 2.

00:01:34.399 --> 00:01:39.890
There was also a hint to Gladiator ally Leap
Frog with a Giant Frogs poster in his workshop.

00:01:39.890 --> 00:01:43.660
In the comics, Gladiator has been both an
ally and villain of Daredevil's.

00:01:43.660 --> 00:01:47.710
So far in the show, he seems to like Daredevil's
work and is on his side.

00:01:47.710 --> 00:01:51.690
But there's been mention before that he's
worked for criminals and those Stilt-Man legs

00:01:51.690 --> 00:01:56.560
and armour have been teased heavily in both
seasons, so it would be awesome to see someone

00:01:56.560 --> 00:02:00.619
like Turk become Stilt-Man, which he once
did in the comics.

00:02:00.619 --> 00:02:03.909
Jon Bernthal's portrayal of the Punisher was
incredible in season 2.

00:02:03.909 --> 00:02:07.170
The finale also cemented his character and
mindset.

00:02:07.170 --> 00:02:11.880
He's cut himself off completely from his old
life burning down his family home and declaring

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:13.920
himself already dead to Karen.

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:18.720
What I really want to see though is for Castle
to use that minigun which I think he will

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:23.230
as did you notice how his hand twitched in
the scene where he uncovers the weapons cache

00:02:23.230 --> 00:02:25.110
and the camera focuses on the minigun?!

00:02:25.110 --> 00:02:30.080
There was also a nice tease for Castle's assistant
Microchip from the comics with the Micro disc

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:32.350
that Castle recovers from his old home.

00:02:32.350 --> 00:02:36.360
By the way, Micro was namedropped in an episode
of Agents of SHIELD and described as a kind

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:39.790
of "crime scene junkie", providing intel to
Skye.

00:02:39.790 --> 00:02:44.710
A team-up with Castle's brutal killing skills
and a computer hacker like Microchip would

00:02:44.710 --> 00:02:50.400
be an awesome combo to see on Daredevil, a
Punisher spin-off or any other Marvel shows.

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:54.420
Wilson Fisk promised Matt Murdock that he
would come after Matt and Foggy when he gets

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:55.470
out of prison.

00:02:55.470 --> 00:02:59.640
Although Fisk was only in season 2 for a small
part, he really made his presence felt when

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:04.060
he did appear and Vincent D'Onofrio played
the crime lord so well that I really want

00:03:04.060 --> 00:03:05.370
to see him back again.

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:09.400
It was pretty terrifying when he smacked Matt
down after Matt threatened to take Vanessa

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:14.030
away from him, and I can't wait to see what
evil plans he has in store for the Avocado

00:03:14.030 --> 00:03:15.030
At Law.

00:03:15.030 --> 00:03:19.250
By the way, in the Born Again comic story
arc, Karen Page, who's become a drug addict,

00:03:19.250 --> 00:03:23.010
sells the information that the identity of
Daredevil is Matt Murdock.

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:27.140
This info eventually reaches the Kingpin who
sets about destroying Matt's life.

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:31.290
It would be cool to see how the TV show might
tackle this storyline.

00:03:31.290 --> 00:03:35.110
We've had some sneaky teases to Bullseye in
both Daredevil seasons.

00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:39.340
The sniper who worked for Fisk in the first
season had a playing card in his gun bag and

00:03:39.340 --> 00:03:43.990
the Metro General hospital coffee cups in
season 2 had playing card designs on them.

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:48.610
Bullseye often used playing cards as weapons
in the comics and has a long history of antagonism

00:03:48.610 --> 00:03:49.640
with Daredevil.

00:03:49.640 --> 00:03:54.390
He was once hired by Maxwell Glenn to kill
Matt Murdock and Foggy Nelson and given that

00:03:54.390 --> 00:03:58.900
the sniper with the playing card in season
1 was under Fisk's control, it's easy to see

00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:02.360
that Bullseye could be brought in as a supervillain
for season 3.

00:04:02.360 --> 00:04:06.971
Karen Page has a chequered history in the
comics and the TV show has hinted at a similarly

00:04:06.971 --> 00:04:09.310
complex background for her in the MCU.

00:04:09.310 --> 00:04:13.490
We got the first full tease of this in the
second season when we finally glimpsed what

00:04:13.490 --> 00:04:16.380
was in the file journalist Ben Urich was keeping
on her.

00:04:16.380 --> 00:04:20.850
The newspaper cutting in the file has a headline
"Mystery Accident Causes Teen Fatality" and

00:04:20.850 --> 00:04:25.370
makes mention of a "young man, Kevin Paxton
Page, of Fagan Corners" who died in a car

00:04:25.370 --> 00:04:27.100
accident for unknown reasons.

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:31.290
The cutting also mentions a man with a grey
military moustache, a girl of eight or nine

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:32.620
crying, and a brother.

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:36.650
The girl is probably Karen and although there's
no record of her having a brother in the comics,

00:04:36.650 --> 00:04:41.780
her father is called Paxton Page and he was
a scientist who was exposed to cobalt radiation

00:04:41.780 --> 00:04:43.900
and became the Daredevil villain Death's Head.

00:04:43.900 --> 00:04:47.710
I don't think we'll see Death's Head appear
on the TV show, but the series is definitely

00:04:47.710 --> 00:04:50.340
hinting at a bigger storyline to explore here.

00:04:50.340 --> 00:04:54.720
I really enjoyed the Jessica Jones tie-in
with Foggy being offered a job by Jeri Hogarth

00:04:54.720 --> 00:04:59.210
to help her law firm with cases involving
super-powered individuals like Jessica Jones.

00:04:59.210 --> 00:05:03.290
I think it could be a cool way to get Foggy
teaming up with Jessica Jones herself.

00:05:03.290 --> 00:05:07.780
And a final bonus thing I'd love to see would
be an Avengers cameo on the show, for example,

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:09.930
what about Tom Holland coming in as Spider-Man?

00:05:09.930 --> 00:05:11.780
I mean, wouldn't that be awesome?!

00:05:11.780 --> 00:05:16.400
I'm not sure the MCU is still quite ready
to fully integrate the movie and TV universes

00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:20.710
in that way yet, but it would be so cool if
they could make it happen at some point!

00:05:20.710 --> 00:05:25.510
So guys, what would you love to see in Daredevil
Season 3, The Defenders, or any of Marvel's

00:05:25.510 --> 00:05:26.950
other shows on Netflix?

00:05:26.950 --> 00:05:29.590
And what did you most enjoy about Season 2?

00:05:29.590 --> 00:05:32.240
Do let me know in the comments below.

00:05:32.240 --> 00:05:35.840
And if you're a fan of Daredevil, I've got
